# ── Foundry (contracts) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
contracts/out/
contracts/cache/
contracts/broadcast/
contracts/foundry.lock
# contracts/lib holds Foundry dependencies. The three that remappings.txt
# resolves against are tracked as submodules so CI can build; anything else
# that lands here (stray `forge install`s) stays ignored.
#
# This used to be a blanket `contracts/lib/`, which meant only
# openzeppelin-contracts-upgradeable survived (a registered submodule
# overrides the ignore). forge-std and openzeppelin-contracts existed on
# dev machines only, so every CI checkout failed to resolve imports and
# `forge build` died — taking the Foundry and Slither jobs with it.
contracts/lib/*
!contracts/lib/forge-std
!contracts/lib/openzeppelin-contracts
!contracts/lib/openzeppelin-contracts-upgradeable
*.gas-snapshot
gas-report.txt

# ── Frontend / app ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
